BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:state-pte-tennessee-2025-04-15@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250415
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250416
SUMMARY:Tennessee: Franchise\, Excise Tax Return (form number commonly FAE1
 70\; not independently confirmed this session) due
DESCRIPTION:Tennessee has no broad individual income tax\, but LLCs and lim
 ited partnerships (along with corporations) doing business in or registered
  in Tennessee must file the Franchise & Excise Tax return\, due the 15th da
 y of the 4th month after year-end - this is TN's primary source of state-le
 vel tax exposure for pass-through entities. | Tennessee has no broad indivi
 dual income tax\, but LLCs and limited partnerships (along with corporation
 s) doing business in or registered in Tennessee must file the Franchise & E
 xcise Tax return\, due the 15th day of the 4th month after year-end - this 
 is TN's primary source of state-level tax exposure for pass-through entitie
 s. Extension mechanism (automatic vs. filed request) not independently conf
 irmed this session. | Authority: Tennessee Department of Revenue\, direct f
 etch this session: "15th day of the fourth month following the close of you
 r books and records. For businesses with a January 1 - December 31 calendar
  year\, this tax is due on April 15 of the following year" and "If you are 
 a corporation\, limited partnership\, limited liability company\, or busine
 ss trust chartered\, qualified\, or registered in Tennessee or doing busine
 ss in this state\, then you must register for and pay franchise and excise 
 taxes." | Source: https://www.tn.gov/revenue/taxes/franchise---excise-tax/d
 ue-dates-and-tax-rates.html | This date is computed from a recurrence rule 
 and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm against the cited so
 urce before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
